{"id":"resp_9e5860d2c5f38200","created_at":1795604753,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_90d2076bf00c5341","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce a review JSON according to schema. Determine assessment: Does shape satisfy requirement? The requirement TRF-035 clause 4.1.1 says L is ship's rule length used by classification society. The candidate shape defines property vocab:ruleLength with node kind IRI pointing to QuantityValue with numericValue decimal and unit metre. That's correct. Also there is classificationSocietyRuleLength property separate but not used. This shape enforces ruleLength exists with unit metre. That matches requirement. No defects? Check SHACL: In sh:property, they set sh:nodeKind sh:IRI, but ruleLength should be IRI? Actually property value should be a node (QuantityValue) which is IRI? In RDF, QuantityValue is a node which is an instance of class. So IRI is fine. The nested shape uses sh:property on that node. Looks okay. Validate: They set sh:minCount 1, but maybe also sh:maxCount? Not required. No datatype constraints on parent property. The nested node shape has sh:property with numericValue decimal minCount 1 and unit has sh:hasValue unit:M and minCount 1. That's good.\n\nPotential issue: they used sh:nodeKind sh:IRI for ruleLength but ruleLength range is QuantityValue (a class). That's acceptable.\n\nPotential missing: need sh:class for QuantityValue? Could be better to enforce sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>. But not required. However maybe they need to enforce that the node is of that class. Not a defect per spec? Could be considered missing constraint but not actionable? The requirement may require that it's a QuantityValue. They use nested shape to enforce properties, that implies it's a QuantityValue (has those properties) but not explicitly sh:class. Could be considered missing but not a code defect? Might be considered lacking sh:class, but acceptable.\n\nThus no actionable code defect. No material gaps? Retrieval gaps listed G1..G5 need assessment. Are they material? They refer to missing source sections, unresolved source documents. These are gaps in source evidence, not code. According to policy, unresolved gaps that are material require question. Are they material? Maybe not affecting shape. Probably UNRESOLVED but not material => can be noted as question? According to schema, need to populate \"questions\" array if unresolved material. They may be UNRESOLVED but not blocking. Might set no questions.\n\ngap_review expects array with objects for each G id with material boolean and why. Must assess each. We need to indicate material false? The gaps pertain to source completeness, but not affecting shape compliance. So we can mark as nonmaterial.\n\nThus assessment = APPROVE (since no defects and all gaps nonmaterial). Provide empty issues array. Provide questions empty. gap_review list with each G and material false, why explanation.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nNeed to include issues field even if empty (must be array). Provide issues: [].\n\nquestions: [].\n\ngap_review: [{id:\"G1\", material:false, why:\"Source section reference not required for SHACL compliance.\"}, ... similar for others].\n\nMake sure IDs match exactly G1..G5.\n\nReturn JSON.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_91544d33d99aa285","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"APPROVE\",\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"gap_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G1\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing citation for section 10 does not affect the correctness of the SHACL shape enforcing the ruleLength requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G2\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing citation for section 3 is unrelated to the shape definition and therefore non‑material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G3\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Ambiguity around Table 3 references does not impact the validation constraints for ruleLength.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G4\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Ambiguity around Table 6 references is not required for the SHACL shape to enforce the ruleLength property.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G5\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing external document (UR P0) is not needed for the shape to satisfy the represented requirement.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":77690,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":576,"cache_write_tokens":77104,"input_tokens_per_turn":[77690],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[576]},"output_tokens":921,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":663,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[921],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":78611},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}